The timer looks at the turn's thread's first place, whatever core's time it holds,
so a thread whose place here was emptied during its turn runs on while its first place holds another core's,
for as long as the timer is deferred.

Caught-by: fuzz-smp2
Report: the timer lets the tick pass that drains the turn's account
Witness: fuzz-smp2 cores-release-across

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -890,7 +890,7 @@ uint32_t sched_wake_ticks(void)
         return 1;
     }
     /* A thread that lost the time of this core during its turn here, its place emptied, ends the turn at the next tick. */
-    const struct place *p = thread_place_on(turn, core_index());
+    const struct place *p = turn->time[0].type == CAP_TIME ? thread_place(turn, 0) : NULL;
     if (core->run_queue != 0 || p == NULL) {
         return 1;
     }
